'''''Rhododendron japonicum''''', the '''Japanese azalea''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Ericaceae]], native to Japan.<ref name="POWO_60454333-2" >{{cite POWO |id=60454333-2 |title=''Rhododendron japonicum'' (A.Gray) Suringar |access-date=13 August 2023 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=''Rhododendron japonicum'' - (Blume.)Schneid.
|website=PFAF Plant Database |url=https://pfaf.org/user/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Rhododendron+japonicum |publisher=Plants for a Future |access-date=13 August 2023 }}</ref> A deciduous shrub reaching {{cvt|8|ft|m|1}} but usually half that, it is found in grasslands and open scrub, never in dense thickets or woodlands.<ref name="treesandshrubsonline" >{{cite web |title=''Rhododendron japonicum'' (A. Gray) Suringar ex Wils. |url=https://www.treesandshrubsonline.org/articles/rhododendron/rhododendron-japonicum |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=Trees and Shrubs Online |publisher=International Dendrology Society |access-date=13 August 2023 }}</ref> It is very similar to the Chinese endemic ''[[Rhododendron molle]]'', to the extent that its cultivars are customarily grouped with the cultivars of ''R.{{nbsp}}molle''.<ref name="treesandshrubsonline" />
It is popularly cultivated as a [[bonsai]] tree.<ref name="bonsaitree">{{Cite web |title=Japanese Azalea Bonsai Tree |work=Love My Bonsai Catalog |access-date=16 November 2023 |url= https://www.lovemybonsai.com/products/japanese-azalea-bonsai-tree }}</ref>
